[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204085 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186203858 :question/id #uuid "aba1787c-af4b-5adc-8302-6302e891978b" :question/math-academy-id "e-17532" :question/problem "Given the function $f(x,y,z,w) = xyzw,$ compute $\\nabla_{x,w} \\: f.$" :question/worked-solution "To compute $\\nabla_{x,w} \\: f$, we take partial derivatives with respect to $x$ and $w$ only.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=\\frac{∂}{∂x}(xyzw) & =yzw \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂w}=\\frac{∂}{∂w}(xyzw) & =xyz\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∇}_{x,w}\\,f & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂w}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}yzw \\\\ xyz\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "efe27056-c688-56de-9859-98464f57ef64" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050143 :topic/difficulty 0.9203935261624193 :topic/encompasses [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186428464 :encompassing/rationale "Initial Codex estimate from captured target-band crossing frequency. Selected account foundations: 1 rises / 1 eligible passed source activities = 1.000000; nearest selected fraction = 1. Crossing activity numbers [1]; waits [1]. Separate account estimates: foundations=1 (1/1). Selection: most observations, then lower weight, then account name; no averaging. Single-activity estimates included. Intervening target updates: False. Crossing frequency is the chosen practical estimate of encompassing coverage; a multi-band rise counts once. This does not interpret color steps as physical repetition units. Method: encompassing-report.md. Evidence: reference/mathacademy/encompassing-analysis-2026-10-11/frequency-fractions/foundations-frequency-estimates.json, pair 1934->1929. All account evidence retained in the prepared import's selected-relationships.json." :encompassing/topic {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048707} :encompassing/weight 1.0} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186428465 :encompassing/rationale 