nt :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186665264} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5fe25d02-d1df-5031-80d6-7a105e6a0e93" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "xy" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186665019}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5fe25d02-d1df-5031-80d6-7a105e6a0e93" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "xy" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186665019} :answer-field/id #uuid "e3125dba-425f-5948-bbd5-415ce14598f4" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186665350}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b8cd5f1c-ad94-59eb-beb3-b7e9e1c7c0ba" :question/math-academy-id "q-264861" :question/problem "Given the function $f(x,y;a,b,c)=ax+by+cxy,$ compute ${∇}_{b,c}\\,f.$\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"30px\">${∇}_{b,c}\\,f=\\text{ }$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "To compute ${∇}_{b,c}\\,f$, we take partial derivatives with respect to $b$ and $c.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂b} & =\\frac{∂}{∂b}(ax+by+cxy)=y \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂c} & =\\frac{∂}{∂c}(ax+by+cxy)=xy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∇}_{b,c}\\,f & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{∂f}{∂b} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂c}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}y \\\\ xy\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186665427 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b216438-f416-5fcc-8b61-88fed5aef51c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186664950}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2b216438-f416-5fcc-8b61-88fed5aef51c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186664950} :answer-field/id #uuid "a0ca1b79-7081-56d7-968e-91958171060d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186665320} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5c492c4b-49c6-517b-a8e5-5c92dcaea23f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "xy" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186665014}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5c492c4b-49c6-517b-a8e5-5c92dcaea23f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "xy" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186665014} :answer-field/id #uuid "f5608b25-e406-5e38-8203-ae875bb76a2b" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186665355}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d00c9169-1416-5517-ab91-db2d056168e6" :question/math-academy-id "q-264860" :question/problem "Given the function $f(x,y;a,b,c)=a{x}^{2}+bxy+c,$ compute ${∇}_{a,b}\\,f.$\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"30px\">${∇}_{a,b}\\,f=\\text{ }$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "To compute ${∇}_{a,b}\\,f$, we take partial derivatives with respect to $a$ and $b.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂a} & =\\frac{∂}{∂a}(a{x}^{2}+bxy+c)={x}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂b} & =\\frac{∂}{∂b}(a{x}^{2}+bxy+c)=xy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∇}_{a,b}\\,f & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{∂f}{∂a} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂b}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}{x}^{2} \\\\ xy\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Computing Parameter Subset Gradients"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204088 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186203860 :question/id #uuid "1639c64c-655b-5822-8464-0f4a704887df" :question/math-academy-id "e-17534" :question/problem "Given the function $f(\\mathbf{x}; \\mathbf{w}) = (w_1x_1 - w_2+x_2)^2,$ compute $\\nabla_{\\mathbf{w}}(\\nabla_{\\mathbf{w}} \\: f).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we compute $\\nabla_{\\mathbf{w}} \\: f$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂{w}_{1}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂{w}_{1}}({w}_{1}{x}_{1}-{w}_{2}+{x}_{2})^{2}=2{x}_{1}({w}_{1}{x}_{1}-{w}_{2}+{x}_{2}) \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂{w}_{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂{w}_{2}}({w}_{1}{x}_{1}-{w}_{2}+{x}_{2})^{2}=-2({w}_{1}{x}_{1}-{w}_{2}+{x}_{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we compute the second derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{w}_{1}^{2}}=2{x}_{1}^{2}\\,\\, &  & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{w}_{1}∂{w}_{2}}=-2{x}_{1} \\\\  & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{w}_{2}∂{w}_{1}}=-2{x}_{1}\\,\\, &  & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{w}_{2}^{2}}=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∇}_{w}({∇}_{w}\\,f) & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{w}_{1}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{w}_{1}∂{w}_{2}} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{w}_{2}∂{w}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{w}_{2}^{2}}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2{x}_{1}^{2} & -2{x}_{1} \\\\ -2{x}_{1} & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "26c6e982-dcf3-5521-84d9-5d8ca8b51a33" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048859 :topic/difficulty 0.4152491812988833 :topic/id #uuid "c6e63ba3-f17e-5d7d-8b1e-f7ca5b0feff7" :topic/knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157423} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157424} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157425}] :topic/math-academy-id 2824 :topic/next [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048637} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048786} {:db/id #edb/ref 175921860