:answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186665318}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "628c0f03-ab55-540e-8220-e8f64d3b5705" :question/math-academy-id "q-264883" :question/problem "Given the function $f(x,y,z)={x}^{2}yz$, compute ${∇}_{y,z}({∇}_{y,z}\\,f).$\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"30px\">${∇}_{y,z}({∇}_{y,z}f)=\\text{ }$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-3}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-4}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "First, we take the variable subset gradient:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∇}_{y,z}\\,f & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}yz) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂z}({x}^{2}yz)\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}{x}^{2}z \\\\ {x}^{2}y\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we compute the second derivatives with respect to $y$ and $z$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}z)=0\\,\\, &  & \\frac{∂}{∂z}({x}^{2}z)={x}^{2} \\\\  & \\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}y)={x}^{2}\\,\\, &  & \\frac{∂}{∂z}({x}^{2}y)=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∇}_{y,z}({∇}_{y,z}\\,f) & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂z} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂z∂y} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{z}^{2}}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & {x}^{2} \\\\ {x}^{2} & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186665436 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "58219723-aa01-5b79-9c02-8f334bdc923f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x_{2}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186665007}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "58219723-aa01-5b79-9c02-8f334bdc923f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x_{2}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186665007} :answer-field/id #uuid "49427f7c-a779-5597-957b-7919756bdf3d" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186665290} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b22662a2-33f9-5d8d-9141-d733f6721f86" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186665143}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b22662a2-33f9-5d8d-9141-d733f6721f86" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186665143} :answer-field/id #uuid "8822fc62-a89d-5971-9ad2-2105b4207d19" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186665310}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e0bc36c0-46f8-5c86-aeeb-c03594b86e35" :question/math-academy-id "q-264904" :question/problem "Given the function $f(x;w)={w}_{1}^{2}{x}_{1}^{2}+{w}_{2}^{2}{x}_{2}^{2}$, compute ${∇}_{w}({∇}_{w}\\,f).$\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"30px\">${∇}_{w}({∇}_{w}\\,f)=\\text{ }$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">$2{x}_{1}^{2}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">$0$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "First, we compute ${∇}_{w}\\,f$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂{w}_{1}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂{w}_{1}}({w}_{1}^{2}{x}_{1}^{2}+{w}_{2}^{2}{x}_{2}^{2})=2{w}_{1}{x}_{1}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂{w}_{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂{w}_{2}}({w}_{1}^{2}{x}_{1}^{2}+{w}_{2}^{2}{x}_{2}^{2})=2{w}_{2}{x}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we compute the second derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{w}_{1}^{2}}=2{x}_{1}^{2}\\,\\, &  & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{w}_{1}∂{w}_{2}}=0 \\\\  & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{w}_{2}∂{w}_{1}}=0\\,\\, &  & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{w}_{2}^{2}}=2{x}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∇}_{w}({∇}_{w}\\,f) & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{w}_{1}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{w}_{1}∂{w}_{2}} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{w}_{2}∂{w}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{w}_{2}^{2}}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2{x}_{1}^{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2{x}_{2}^{2}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Computing Second-Order Derivatives"}]
